      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Switching to hardware security keys eliminates SIM-swapping attacks and SMS interception, which are the most exploited vectors in social engineering attacks. By using YubiKeys, you leverage FIDO2 protocol standards that use public/private key cryptography, rendering traditional password resets and intercepted codes completely ineffective against hackers. This fundamentally closes the \"broken ACL\" vulnerabilities where attackers can monitor network traffic or intercept low-security codes to gain unauthorized access.",
