      "content": "To prevent loss and frustration, implement a dual-authentication recovery process where each key pairs with a personal device (like a mobile phone or laptop) stored in a secure, shared company drive or password-protected network folder, ensuring staff can regenerate access if a key breaks or gets lost. Pair this with a \"just-in-time\" support model where the IT team provides in-person or video onboarding sessions specifically for non-technical staff before the official rollout date, treating the training like a standard procedural session rather than a tech demo. Finally, offer a one-month \"grace period\" where both the key and SMS remain supported to allow users to practice logging in with the new device and become comfortable before SMS is fully deprecated for all clients.",
